[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says: one issue, one fix queued. It was merged on subject lines
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every subject says "wrong day". Read by
tenant, by channel and by what each report says, it holds three problems.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed, and booking-v3's form is retired instead
of fixed. That settles two of the three problems. Nothing in that update touches the third.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but its reports are not all answered: dates that move by one day are still open.
</Callout>

## One ticket per problem

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} {states} />

The tickets:

- [support-kb-4471#1](https://github.com/yazon/support-kb-4471/issues/1) · `parser`
- [support-kb-4471#2](https://github.com/yazon/support-kb-4471/issues/2) · `hint`
- [support-kb-4471#3](https://github.com/yazon/support-kb-4471/issues/3) · `one-day`

## parser: the shared parser reads month first

Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. The shared parser reads every date month first, so day
and month come out swapped: "Booked for 2 December. The invite says 12 February." It reaches people
through the app, by email and through booking-v2's form.

**Fixed:** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`, with #4471 closed on 5 October. Ticket closed as
completed.

## hint: booking-v3 asks for the month first

Same symptom, different code. booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at a
day-first tenant type what the hint tells them, and the form reads it day first, the tenant's way.
Only reports through booking-v3's form, from the tenants that run it.

**Won't fix:** booking-v3's form is retired. The parser fix does not touch this form, so these reports
end with the form, not with a fix. Ticket closed as not planned.

## one-day: dates move by one day

A swap of day and month cannot move a date by one day, and these reports describe exactly that:

- "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May."
- "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting."
- "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday."

The desk read them as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). [CauseTable](/kb/incidents/4471) files
them under `parser` by tenant, with a footnote; nothing else ever came of the footnote. The Lisbon and
Toronto report points at a time zone: a date turned into an instant and back in the wrong zone.

**Open:** neither the parser fix nor retiring booking-v3 moves a date back by one day. Investigate the
time-zone handling of invite dates; the ticket stays open until then.

## How the counts are made

With the desk's own view, as CauseTable counts: one report per id, each counted under the cause its
tenant and channel give it (`causes.ts`). The reports the desk read as a one-day move stay counted
where they're filed, under `parser`, and are the one-day ticket's count as well. Intake's tags are not
used: they are guessed from the reporter's browser.

## Lessons

- Same subject is not same cause. Merge by cause, and read the body before you call a ticket known.
- A footnote under a table is a ticket nobody filed.

